  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "27238714105933bc7e1b484c1bb2e7983f6391b9",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2401558725,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The weird thing is that, apart from the mention in [RFC 8335 section 6](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8335#section-6), there is **NO** mention of the Extension Structure anywhere for the ICMP Extended Echo _Reply_ message. So, it's not even defined how it is be included in the ICMP Extended Echo _Reply_ message (see figure 3 and the following text). That's probably why this is not in the dissector. Is this a bug in the RFC?\n\nThere's a [draft](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-intarea-rfc8335bis/) out there, which seem to address this though...",
          "author": {
            "id": 2398962,
            "username": "JaapKeuter",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jaap Keuter",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/722b0c520542a23cb8f8ea7070a45c88f9e9214dc700ac151e419e9649e0304e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/JaapKeuter"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-03-17T20:00:21.867Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-03-17T20:06:57.275Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 369712048,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 19325,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3345250dd6d439740fd125b7f2fde8e36cefc47d",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2401612683,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Thank you for the response! \n\nI agree with your assessment. I simply thought that\n\n>   Many ICMP messages are extensible as currently defined.  Protocol designers can extend ICMP messages by simply appending fields or data structures to them.\n\nwould cover the situation here where a person would use an extended echo response as a means to include \"related\" data.\n\nThat said ... I knew that the authors were \"cleaning up\" some things from the first draft. I am not surprised that this issue is something that they addressed. \n\nFrom my first read, it looks like the draft handles it in a way that this MR would work. Do you agree with that reading? I am working with the draft authors on some other work and I could speak to them to confirm, if need be.\n\nThank you (again) for the response!\nWill",
          "author": {
            "id": 8950053,
            "username": "hawkinsw",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Will Hawkins",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/8950053/avatar.png?v=1768994429",
